        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405">

                <pb facs="0938" n="898" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v09p1/pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">784A.5 MSP/2–2752:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 405<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Israel (Davis) to the Department of State</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d405-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tel
                                Aviv</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-02-27T18:00:00+02:00">February 27, 1952—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>881. Enlarging on info from FonMin (Embtel 880, February 27) that GOI has recd indication of Jordanian interest in
                    possible modification Arab attitude toward Israel, Michael Comay, Acting DirGen
                    FonOff gave me fol details which he requested
                    we treat as confidential for obvious reasons. He identified Jordanian source as
                    Ahmed Touqan Jordan’s rep on MAC saying latter
                    had expressed desire have informal talk with S Divon, Acting Dir ME Div Israel
                        FonOff who met him in Jerusalem Monday
                    February 25 for that purpose.</p>
                <p>According to Comay, Touqan indicated that PriMin Abulhuda had expressed interest in
                    possibility of some change in attitude of <pb facs="0939" n="899" xml:id="pg899"
                    /> Arab League toward Israel and thought matter might come up at meeting
                    scheduled for latter part March. His interest was based on (1) more moderate
                    tone noted in recent Egyptian pronouncements relating to Israel, and (2) fact
                    that publicity in this sense in Jordan had elicited no expression of public
                    disapproval.</p>
                <p>Comay stated further that rep Leb Govt had expressed interest in having
                    conversation with Makleff, who until
                    recently was deputy chief of staff. Since latter now England Major Gen.
                        Yadin, chief of staff, replied he wld
                    be glad take part in conversations personally. His offer was accepted and mtg
                    has been arranged for tomorrow, Thursday February 28 at Rea En Nakoura.
                        Comay said there was nothing very
                    definite about either of these developments but he thought US Govt wld be
                    interested nevertheless.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d405-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d405-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Paris, London, Ankara, Beirut, Damascus, Amman, Cairo, Baghdad, and
                    Jerusalem.</p>
            </note>
